  user_input {
    user_response: "You are a Principal Software Architect and Local SEO specialist. I am prototyping a Local SEO Geo-Grid Rank Tracker and Prospecting SaaS (similar to ProfitMaps AI / Local Falcon).\n\nBefore we build the full web application, I need you to implement and validate the foundational core engine logic in clean, modular TypeScript:\n\n1. Coordinate Grid Generator Function:\n   - Takes: Center coordinate (latitude, longitude), Grid Size (e.g., 3x3, 5x5, 7x7), and Distance Step (e.g., in kilometers or miles).\n   - Returns: An array of coordinate points with their row/col indices and exact calculated lat/long offsets using proper geodesic math (Haversine/equirectangular approximation suitable for local radii).\n\n2. DataForSEO / SERP API Local Maps Rank Parser:\n   - Provide a sample parser function that accepts:\n     - Target business identifiers: Place ID, Business Name, or Domain URL.\n     - A mocked Google Local/Maps SERP response array of 20 items (name, place_id, address, rating, reviews, rank_position).\n   - Returns: Pin scan result with `rank` (1-20, or >20 if not found), top 3 competing businesses, and status color tag (`green` for 1-3, `yellow` for 4-10, `red` for 11+).\n\n3. Local SEO AI Audit & Pitch Generator (Structured Output):\n   - Write a Gemini prompt and a Zod schema/JSON output structure that takes:\n     - Target Business Name & Category\n     - Overall Grid Metric (Average rank, % in Top 3, Total scanned nodes)\n     - Top 3 dominant competitors in the red/weak zones\n   - Returns structured JSON:\n     - `executiveSummary`: High-impact summary of their visibility loss.\n     - `missedRevenueEstimate`: Explaining why being out of the top 3 costs calls.\n     - `actionPlan`: 4 tactical fixes (GBP categories, citations, reviews, on-page localized content).\n     - `coldOutreachPitch`: A personalized, conversational cold email / direct mail hook an agency can send to the business owner citing these exact grid statistics.\n\nPlease output the complete, tested TypeScript code for items 1 and 2, along with the prompt template and sample JSON output for item 3."
    items {
      text: "You are a Principal Software Architect and Local SEO specialist. I am prototyping a Local SEO Geo-Grid Rank Tracker and Prospecting SaaS (similar to ProfitMaps AI / Local Falcon).\n\nBefore we build the full web application, I need you to implement and validate the foundational core engine logic in clean, modular TypeScript:\n\n1. Coordinate Grid Generator Function:\n   - Takes: Center coordinate (latitude, longitude), Grid Size (e.g., 3x3, 5x5, 7x7), and Distance Step (e.g., in kilometers or miles).\n   - Returns: An array of coordinate points with their row/col indices and exact calculated lat/long offsets using proper geodesic math (Haversine/equirectangular approximation suitable for local radii).\n\n2. DataForSEO / SERP API Local Maps Rank Parser:\n   - Provide a sample parser function that accepts:\n     - Target business identifiers: Place ID, Business Name, or Domain URL.\n     - A mocked Google Local/Maps SERP response array of 20 items (name, place_id, address, rating, reviews, rank_position).\n   - Returns: Pin scan result with `rank` (1-20, or >20 if not found), top 3 competing businesses, and status color tag (`green` for 1-3, `yellow` for 4-10, `red` for 11+).\n\n3. Local SEO AI Audit & Pitch Generator (Structured Output):\n   - Write a Gemini prompt and a Zod schema/JSON output structure that takes:\n     - Target Business Name & Category\n     - Overall Grid Metric (Average rank, % in Top 3, Total scanned nodes)\n     - Top 3 dominant competitors in the red/weak zones\n   - Returns structured JSON:\n     - `executiveSummary`: High-impact summary of their visibility loss.\n     - `missedRevenueEstimate`: Explaining why being out of the top 3 costs calls.\n     - `actionPlan`: 4 tactical fixes (GBP categories, citations, reviews, on-page localized content).\n     - `coldOutreachPitch`: A personalized, conversational cold email / direct mail hook an agency can send to the business owner citing these exact grid statistics.\n\nPlease output the complete, tested TypeScript code for items 1 and 2, along with the prompt template and sample JSON output for item 3."
    }
  }
}
