  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Technical Direction**\n\nI\'m focusing on the implementation details now. My primary concern is updating `metadata.json` and `index.html`. For clean structuring, I\'m starting to create `src/engine/geoGrid.ts`, which I\'ll build using a high-precision Geodesic coordinate grid generator. This generator needs equirectangular local projection and geodesic Vincenty / Haversine inverse abilities.\n\n\n**Defining Grid Calculations**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the `geoGrid.ts` file, and working on the grid offsetting logic, focusing on metric and imperial units. I\'m nailing down the input/output types and helper math for the functions: `haversineDistance()` and `calculateDestinationPoint()`. I\'m starting to visualize how the data will be structured.\n\n\n**Analyzing Rank Tracking Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating an interface for parsing SERP data specifically for local map results, focusing on handling Google\'s local 20-pack. I\'m focusing on the `SerpLocalItem` interface for now. This involves handling place IDs, URLs, and fuzzy name matching to identify target listings. The goal is a clean `PinScanResult` output to track ranking changes. I\'m starting to build out a normalized match criteria.\n\n\n**Developing AI Audit Output**\n\nI\'m now expanding the AI audit and pitch generator to handle structured outputs using Zod schema validation. The current focus is designing the prompt template to incorporate factors such as local SEO domain authority and GBP category relevancy. I\'m aiming for outputs that are well-structured and include review velocity data for a robust AI Audit. I am considering data from mock Google Maps SERP data.\n\n\n**Crafting Outreach Strategies**\n\nI\'m now deep into designing the AI\'s cold outreach output. I\'m focusing on crafting a compelling subject line and personalized email body that highlights the grid rank stats and competitor presence for the client. I\'m considering structuring this data to address missed revenue concerns and formulating an action plan.\n\n\n**Designing Sales Process**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a concise follow-up script for prospecting, considering a multi-touch approach. I\'ve integrated a high-quality sample JSON output from the Gemini `Type.OBJECT` responseSchema for the `@google/genai` backend call. I\'m finalizing the structure to ensure it\'s effective for sales interactions.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
